      "B": "Reject the special order entirely — the $90 price represents a 25% discount below the standard $120 price, the exclusivity clause constrains Meridian's pricing flexibility for three years, and the 20% probability of regular-customer price concessions creates a contingent liability of approximately $72,000 in expected margin loss. Protecting the existing customer base and price integrity is more important than a one-time volume opportunity.",
