    "ItemType": "MCQ",
    "ItemStyle": "single-select",
    "Stem": "Grant & Chen LLP is the external auditor for Harbor Logistics, a publicly traded third-party logistics provider. Harbor uses a SaaS-based transportation management system (TMS) called RouteCloud to process all shipping transactions, calculate freight charges, and generate customer invoices. RouteCloud processes approximately 1.2 million transactions per month representing $34M in revenue. As part of the integrated audit under PCAOB AS 2201, the engagement team must determine whether to rely on RouteCloud's SOC 2 Type II report for IT general controls testing. The team has obtained RouteCloud's SOC 2 Type II report covering the period January 1 through September 30. The report contains: (Finding 1) Backup Failure Exception — the service auditor noted that during March, RouteCloud's automated database backup process failed for 6 days, and the failure was not detected until a customer reported data unavailability on day 7; RouteCloud management's response states that manual backups were performed on days 4-7 and that monitoring alerts have been enhanced; the exception is in the Availability trust services category; (Finding 2) Access Recertification Gap — quarterly user access reviews for RouteCloud employees with administrative privileges were completed for Q1 and Q3 but not Q2; the service auditor noted that 14 administrative accounts that should have been reviewed in Q2 remained active without review for 6 months; RouteCloud management's response states that Q2 recertification was delayed by a system migration and has since been completed; the exception is in the Security trust services category; (Finding 3) Change Management Deviation — 3 of 45 sampled production changes (7%) were deployed without evidence of peer review or post-implementation testing; RouteCloud management's response states that these were emergency patches for a critical security vulnerability and that a retrospective review confirmed no adverse impact; the exception is in the Processing Integrity trust services category. The engagement partner has asked the audit team to analyze whether these three findings preclude reliance on the SOC 2 Type II report. Which of the following conclusions is most appropriate?",
    "CorrectChoice": "C",
    "ExplanationCorrect": "The SOC 2 Type II report cannot be relied upon without additional procedures because all three findings affect trust services categories that are directly relevant to the audit of Harbor's financial statements. The analysis requires the auditor to evaluate each finding against the COSO-based framework for service organization controls: (1) Availability — the 6-day backup failure creates a 7-day window where Harbor's transaction data completeness cannot be assured; during this period, 280,000 transactions ($7.9M in revenue) may have incomplete or lost data; the auditor must perform additional procedures to verify the completeness of Harbor's transaction records during this specific window; (2) Security — the Q2 access recertification gap means the auditor cannot rely on RouteCloud's access controls for a 6-month period; with 14 unreviewed administrative accounts during that period, the risk of unauthorized changes to the TMS configuration (freight rate tables, invoice calculation logic) is elevated; (3) Processing Integrity — the 7% change management deviation rate exceeds the typical tolerable deviation rate for ITGC testing; the emergency-patch rationale may be valid, but the absence of post-implementation testing means the auditor cannot rely on the change management control during the affected period. The SOC reporting analysis principle tested is that a Type II report with exceptions in trust-services categories relevant to the user entity's financial reporting requires the user auditor to perform additional procedures — the report does not provide audit evidence for the controls during the exception periods.",
    "SourceDescription": "Original CMA Part 1 exam-style practice. Not real CMA exam content and not copied from official samples.",
