    "ExplanationWrongB": "Granting all department managers full access to all ERP modules would eliminate segregation of duties entirely — it is the opposite of what COSO Principle 10 requires. Segregation of duties works by dividing incompatible functions across different individuals so that no single person can both perpetrate and conceal errors or fraud. Full access for everyone means any manager could create a fictitious vendor, approve a purchase order, and modify receipt quantities — precisely the risks the auditor identified. The goal is not to distribute blame but to prevent unilateral action through system-enforced role separation.",
